Q: Google Play Console warning: libstaticwebp.so 16KB issue in Fresco A: <p>The default react-native Image component depends on the above library even after removing all the third-party libraries. While checking the GitHub issues, I observed that version 3.4.0 has  solved the issue. We can check the issue solution at ( <a href="https://github.com/facebook/fresco/releases/tag/v3.4.0" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://github.com/facebook/fresco/releases/tag/v3.4.0</a> )</p>
<p>In the project-level build.gradle file, add the below configuration to override/choose the above version.</p>
<pre><code>allprojects {
    configurations.all {
        resolutionStrategy {
            // Force Fresco to v3.4.0 or higher for 16KB support
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:fresco:3.4.0&quot;
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:imagepipeline-okhttp3:3.4.0&quot;
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:ui-common:3.4.0&quot;
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:imagepipeline:3.4.0&quot;
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:drawee:3.4.0&quot;
            // If you still see webp errors, force these specifically:
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:webpsupport:3.4.0&quot;
            force &quot;com.facebook.fresco:animated-webp:3.4.0&quot;
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>Once done, build the aab again. The error would be gone upon aab inspection.</p>
